# Security and privacy

## OWASP
- All DB access through **Prisma** (no string-concat SQL).
- Auth on every mutation. Authorize by role (see implementation plan matrix).
- Never commit `.env`, keys, or customer dumps.
- CSRF: Next.js Server Actions / same-site cookies. No open CORS.
- Uploads: type/size limits; do not serve user files as executable.
- Rate-limit login. Hash passwords with a modern KDF (Auth.js defaults).

## NDPR (customer data)
- Collect only fields the workflow needs (name, phone, address, measurements).
- No public customer list. Sales/owner/manager only.
- Audit logs for order, payment, inventory, production, QC, overrides.
- Do not log raw passwords, full card data, or unnecessary PII in console or `AuditLog` payloads.

Workers see **assigned tasks**, not the full customer directory.
